    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d718">

                <pb facs="0838" n="552" sameAs="frus:frus1916Supp/pg552"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 165.102/857</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Great Britain</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Page</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">London</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1916-02-25T14:00:00+00:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">February 25, 1916, 2 p. m.</hi>
                        </date>
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received 8 p. m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>3850. Your 2915, February 21, 9 p. m. I have unofficially approached Foreign
                    Office and requested permit. They state that they do not issue actual permits in
                    London but give orders to the Consul General at Rotterdam to issue permit upon
                    the application of shippers when goods reach Rotterdam. They consider that their
                    undertaking not to interfere with shipment of dyes to the United States as
                    expressed in their note of January 28, cabled to the Department in my 3668 of
                    January 31 [29]<anchor n="1" xml:id="d718-f1"/> is the same as permit.</p>
                <closer>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Embassy</hi>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d718-f1" n="1" xml:id="d718-f1-content">
                <p>Not printed; see the Ambassador’s despatch No. 2967, January 31, <hi
                        rendition="#italic">ante</hi>, <ref target="#pg551">p. 551</ref>.</p>
            </note>
